Package: bmassa
Title: Biomass of Aquatic Taxa from Abundances and Body Sizes
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pablo", "Amador Crespo", email = "pamadorc@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3793-8794")),
    person("Andreu", "Rico", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1820-4218"))
  )
Description: Estimates the mean individual mass and the biomass of aquatic
    taxa (phytoplankton, zooplankton, macroinvertebrates, fish and
    amphibians) from abundance data, with prediction intervals. Hierarchical
    models fitted to published compilations and data sets of typical masses,
    biovolumes and length-mass relations predict each taxon from its own data
    or, when it is absent, from its closest relatives in the taxonomy of the
    Catalogue of Life, with the uncertainty of that substitution. Totals by
    site keep the correlations between taxa. The reference values come from
    sources listed with their citation, DOI and licence by
    cite_sources(), among them Kremer et al. (2014)
    <doi:10.1890/14-0603.1>, Dumont et al. (1975) <doi:10.1007/BF00377592>,
    Moreau et al. (2021) <doi:10.3897/BDJ.9.e70214> and van Leeuwen et al.
    (2025) <doi:10.1111/fwb.70056>; phytoplankton carbon follows
    Menden-Deuer and Lessard (2000) <doi:10.4319/lo.2000.45.3.0569>.
